---
// H3 About our AI assistant (English): the Article 50 disclosure in the help template, translated
// from /nl/legal/ai-assistent. Escalation reply within 4 office hours (docs/relaunch/01-besluiten.md
// §15); no supplier names (§8). Copy awaits Frans's sign-off, together with the Dutch text.
import HsLayout from '../../../layouts/HsLayout.astro';
import HsHelp from '../../../components/hs/HsHelp.astro';
import HsIcon from '../../../components/hs/HsIcon.astro';
import { SITE, SITE_EN } from '../../../data/site';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/en' }];
---

<HsLayout
  lang="en"
  title="About our AI assistant"
  seoTitle="About the AI assistant of AI Heroes"
  description="About the AI assistant of AI Heroes: what it can and cannot do, what happens to your data, how it is built and how to reach a person."
  noindex
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <HsHelp
    title="You are chatting with *AI*"
    current="About our AI assistant"
    intro="The assistant on this site is an AI system we built ourselves. Here is what it can do, what happens to your data and how to reach a person."
    updated="October 2026"
    crumbs={crumbs}
    summary={[
      'The assistant is AI, and it says so in the conversation.',
      'It answers from our own pages and names the source.',
      'A person is always within reach through “Talk to a human”.',
      'Processing and storage take place within the EU.',
      'We only ask for your name and email address if you want contact, with your consent.',
    ]}
    toc={[
      { id: 'can', label: 'What the assistant can do' },
      { id: 'data', label: 'Data and retention' },
      { id: 'built', label: 'How it is built' },
      { id: 'person', label: 'Rather talk to a human' },
    ]}
    related={[{ label: 'Privacy statement', href: '/en/legal/privacy' }, { label: 'The case: our own assistant', href: '/en/cases/eigen-stack' }, { label: 'Software you control', href: '/en/self-hosted' }]}
  >
    <div class="hs-prose">
      <p>The chat assistant on aiheroes.io is an AI system, built by AI Heroes itself. We say so in the conversation as well: you always know you are talking to AI, as Article 50 of the European AI Act requires. The assistant is an example of what we build for clients.</p>

      <h2 id="can">What the assistant can do, and what it cannot</h2>
      <p>The assistant answers questions about what we build, the start sprint, our cases, the team, the articles and the AI Salon. It takes you to the right page, helps you book a conversation with the team and hands the conversation over to a person if you want.</p>
      <p>It only gives prices that are also on the site. Answers can be incomplete or wrong; check important information on the page it refers to.</p>

      <h2 id="data">Data and retention</h2>
      <p>Your chat history is stored in your own browser. On our servers we keep conversations pseudonymised, without name, IP address or profile, to improve the assistant, for at most 30 days. Only when you leave your name and email address to get in touch do we process personal data; we keep it for at most 90 days, in line with our <a href="/en/legal/privacy">privacy statement</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="built">How it is built</h2>
      <p>The assistant searches our own pages and answers only on that basis, with the source included. It runs in Frankfurt, with a database in the EU. The language model can be switched without rebuilding the assistant, and every new version first has to pass a fixed test set. That way we do ourselves what we advise clients: compliance from the drawing board and <a href="/en/self-hosted">software you control</a>. Read more in <a href="/en/cases/eigen-stack">the case</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="person">Rather talk to a human?</h2>
      <p>Use “Talk to a human” in the chat. During office hours we reply within 4 hours. You can also email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>; we reply to email within {SITE_EN.reply}.</p>
    </div>
    <p>
      <button class="hs-btn hs-btn--dark" type="button" data-open-chat>
        Open the assistant
        <HsIcon name="arrow-right" />
      </button>
    </p>
  </HsHelp>
</HsLayout>

<script>
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-open-chat]').forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', () => window.dispatchEvent(new Event('aih:open-chat'))),
    );
  });
</script>
